# Test: bgp-redistribute -- emit-burst N=500 add events drives 500 distinct UPDATEs.
# VALIDATES: AC-13 -- consumer/producer paths sustain 500 sequential emissions
#            without dropping events or exceeding the UpdateRoute timeout.
# PREVENTS: Pool sizing bug or per-event allocation hot path causing drops.

stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER
option=tcp_connections:value=1
# 60s, raised from 30s. NOT a relaxation: until 2026-07-16 this test's peer never
# bound, so no UPDATE was ever sent and the 30s only had to cover the .run script's
# own sleeps. Now that all 500 UPDATEs really cross the wire the run measures a
# steady 29.1-29.2s (4/4 runs), which left 0.8s of headroom under the old ceiling.
option=timeout:value=60s
# AC-13 is "500 sequential emissions without dropping events", so all 500
# UPDATEs are enumerated: ze-peer fails on any received UPDATE that matches no
# expectation, so this asserts EXACTLY the 500 emitted prefixes arrive, no more
# and no fewer. Each is ORIGIN incomplete, empty AS_PATH (iBGP), NEXT_HOP
# 127.0.0.4 (ze's OWN address on this session, what `nhop self` resolves to, not
# the peer's 127.0.0.1), LOCAL_PREF 100 (well-known mandatory on iBGP, RFC 4271 5.1.5,
# emitted by reactor_api_batch.go buildWireModeUpdate), NLRI 10.0.0.<i>/32.
# Generated, do not hand-edit: prefixes are 10.0.0.0/32 + i for i in 0..499.
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00310200000015400101024002004003047F00000440050400000064200A000000
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=2:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00310200000015400101024002004003047F00000440050400000064200A000001
expect=bgp:conn=1:seq=3:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF00310200000015400101024002004003047F00000440050400000064200A000002
